    "narrative": "The primary engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 85.81. Facing the vulnerable G. Holmes (xERA 4.65), **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a premium #2 lineup slot and a favorable platoon advantage, maximizing his potential to capitalize on his elite sprint speed\u2014our scarcest and most coveted category. We are also leaning heavily on **Seiya Suzuki** (68.79) and **Mickey Moniak** (65.84). **Mickey Moniak** is a particularly interesting start; despite drawing a tough matchup against L. Webb (xERA 3.96), his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and spot in the #3 hole make him a high-efficiency play for RBI production today.\n\nThe lineup construction remains focused on exploiting pitching weaknesses, as seen with **Josh Naylor** (72.72) drawing a lucrative matchup against the struggling Wesneski. While **Austin Riley** carries a slightly lower score (60.98) due to being pushed down to the #8 spot, his strong SP skill rating (+17%) and the added theft potential against E. Rodriguez provide sufficient upside to start. The most difficult decision remained keeping **Jose Caballero** on the bench; while his base metrics were competitive, his projected #5 lineup position and specific platoon splits against Fisher yielded a sub-zero score relative to our starting options. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** and **Trevor Story**, who remain sidelined on the IL, while **Brice Turang**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** stay on the periphery awaiting rotation shifts. **Travis Bazzana** (45.07) is our riskiest play today; his efficiency is hampered by a L/L platoon disadvantage against W. Peralta, making him a candidate to be pulled if we need to preserve games later in the week.",
